        <body>
            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0844" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg750"/>

                <head>No. 489.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Connery to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-01"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 1, 1887</date>.
                        (Received October 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 233.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with my No. 228 of 26th
                    ultimo, I have the honor to inclose herewith translation of a note from Mr.
                    Mariscal, dated September 27, 1887, acknowledging mine of the previous day,
                    which conveyed to the Mexican Government your congratulations on the prospect of
                    an amicable adjustment of pending difficulties between Mexico and Guatemala.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas B.
                    Connery.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d489-a1.xml" xpointer="d489-a1"/>
